{
  "comment": "Live-mode relevance labels: queryId (from queries.json) → real bookIds in Artem's library. Rebuilt 2026-07-12 against the FULL library index (777/795 books, 309k chunks). LABELING RULE: topic-level relevance — a book is labeled relevant when its SUBJECT covers the query's concept, derived from index metadata, NOT from what search returned (that would be circular and make recall trivially 1.0). A real library has dozens of books per topic (64 cover Rust), so label sets are broad and recall@5 is capped at min(|relevant|, 5) — see metrics.ts. Queries the library genuinely cannot answer (bees, borscht, chess, spaceflight, RU grammar, all neg-*) carry NO labels on purpose: they are LIVE NEGATIVES, scored by lowConfidence. KNOWN THIN AREAS (expected misses, not bugs): HTTP caching (3 books) and compilers/interpreters (2 books) — sp-07 and sp-10 are honest misses that the eval should keep reporting. STATUS: model-proposed from a live probe of all 44 library-scope queries; Artem to spot-check.",
